  "articles": [
    {
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "Mr. Allen has just arrived in Germany."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 2,
      "text": "At the hotel where he is staying he asks the clerk where the cathedral, palace, museum, etc., are and if there is a restaurant downtown near by."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 3,
      "text": "The clerk answers his questions, shows him the locations on the map of the city and tells him how to get to the various buildings."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 4,
      "text": "Mr. Allen goes through customs."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 5,
      "text": "The official asks him where he comes from, where he is going and what he has to declare."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 6,
      "text": "Mr. Allen does not always understand and has to ask the official to repeat and speak slowly."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 7,
      "text": "He tells the official then how many cigars, cigarettes, etc., he has."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 8,
      "text": "Mr. Schneider meets Mr. Keller, whom he hasn't seen for a long time."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 9,
      "text": "Mr. Keller often has to go to Frankfurt but he's staying in Munich for two months now."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 10,
      "text": "He asks Mr. Schneider if he'd like to go and eat."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 11,
      "text": "Mr. Schneider knows a restaurant on Bahnhofstrasse where they go and order Bratwurst and Sauerkraut and beer to drink."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 12,
      "text": "Mr. Keller buys some cigars too."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 13,
      "text": "Mr. Köhler meets Mr. Becker at the hotel to show him the town."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 14,
      "text": "Mr. Becker is not acquainted with the city, but he would like to see the museum, cathedral, palace, city hall, Hofbräuhaus, Ratskeller, park, Königsplatz, etc."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 15,
      "text": "They take a bus through town, and Mr. Köhler points out the sights."
    }
  ],
